---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import sources from '../data/sources.json';
import provenance from '../data/provenance.json';
const retrieved = new Date(provenance.retrievedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---
<Shell title="Sources & methodology" active="sources"><article class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">Follow the reference</span><h1>Sources & methodology</h1><p>The calculator uses only structural Quran metadata: the 114 chapters, their ayah counts, and the 604-page Hafs page layout.</p><h2>What this app quotes</h2><p>Chapter names, ayah counts and the 604-page Hafs layout were retrieved from <a href="https://mcp.quran.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quran Foundation’s official Quran MCP <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a> structural metadata. The calculator quotes no Quran text, commentary or hadith.</p><h2>What is editorial</h2><p>Pace, revision cycles and the schedule are a model built from the numbers you enter. None of it is a ruling or an opinion from quran.ai, Quran.com or Quran Foundation, and no independent scholarly review is claimed.</p><h2>Limits</h2><p>The calculator makes no prediction about anyone’s ability to memorise. Other printed layouts have different page counts, and a plan is best adjusted with a teacher.</p><h2>Snapshot and reuse</h2><p>Canonical snapshot retrieved on {retrieved}. Source records, checksums and edition names ship with the project. Original application code is MIT licensed. DM Sans, Newsreader and Amiri are hosted locally under the SIL Open Font License, with their licence files included.</p><p class="micro">Snapshot SHA-256: <code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">{provenance.snapshotSha256}</code><br />App content SHA-256: <code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">{provenance.appContentSha256}</code></p><h2>References used in this app</h2><p>{sources.length} linked sources. Each opens the source provider in a new tab.</p><ul class="source-list">{sources.map(source=><li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.label} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a> <small>{source.kind}{'note' in source && source.note ? ` · ${source.note}` : ''}</small></li>)}</ul><div class="actions top-gap"><a class="button" href="/">Return to the activity <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a> <button class="button secondary" data-print>Print source notes</button></div></article></Shell>
